# Build-context policy for deploy/gcp/Dockerfile (BuildKit uses
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile). It is an ALLOWLIST:
# everything is excluded, then only the paths the image needs are let back in.
# The Dockerfile additionally copies these paths one by one (no `COPY . .`).

# 1. exclude everything (.git, .env files, secrets, credentials, databases,
#    logs, caches, installer output, screenshots, Claude/session files, ...)
*

# 2. the central-server import closure (= deploy/windows/server-files.txt)
!LICENSE
!deskmate/__init__.py
!deskmate/zaza/__init__.py
!deskmate/zaza/sync/__init__.py
!deskmate/zaza/sync/protocol.py
!deskmate/zaza_server

# 3. the container's own build inputs
!deploy/gcp/requirements-server.lock.txt
!deploy/gcp/entrypoint.sh

# 4. never, even inside the allowed paths
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.zip
**/.git*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.claude*
**/secret
**/secrets
**/*.json
**/*.jsonl
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.log
**/*.output
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
